+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
+<!-- K-Mod hints -->
+	<!-- Style guidelines (from CIV4GameText_Strategy.xml): -->
+	<!-- Technologies should be colored COLOR_TECH_TEXT (example: [COLOR_TECH_TEXT]Bronze Working[COLOR_REVERT]) -->
+	<!-- Unit should be colored COLOR_UNIT_TEXT (example: [COLOR_UNIT_TEXT]Archers[COLOR_REVERT]) -->
+	<!-- Buildings should be colored COLOR_BUILDING_TEXT (example: [COLOR_BUILDING_TEXT]Theatre[COLOR_REVERT]) -->
+	<!-- Projects should be colored COLOR_PROJECT_TEXT (example: [COLOR_PROJECT_TEXT]SS Engine[COLOR_REVERT]) -->
+	<!-- Anything else official (that should be capitalized) should be colored COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT (example: [COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]Trade Mission[COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT] or [COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]Islam[COLOR_HIGHLIGHT_TEXT]) -->
+<Civ4GameText xmlns="http://www.firaxis.com">
+<TEXT>
+	<Tag>TXT_KEY_BUG_HINT_INTERFACE_1</Tag>
+	<English>Press [ALT + CTRL + O] to open The BUG options screen.</English>
+	<French>Pressez [ALT + CTRL + O] pour acc�der aux �crans d'options du BUG Mod.</French>
+	<German>Mit der Tastenkombination [STRG + ALT + O] l�sst sich das Optionsmen� der BUG Mod aufrufen.</German>
+	<Italian>Premi [ALT + CTRL + O] per accedere alla schermata di configurazione del BUG Mod.</Italian>
+	<Spanish>Press [ALT + CTRL + O] to open The BUG options screen.</Spanish>
+</TEXT>
+<TEXT>
+	<Tag>TXT_KEY_KMOD_HINT_1</Tag>
+	<English>An aqueduct or a hospital will increase a city's health, but public transport or a recycling center will reduce its pollution...</English>
+	<French>An aqueduct or a hospital will increase a city's health, but public transport or a recycling center will reduce its pollution...</French>
+	<German>An aqueduct or a hospital will increase a city's health, but public transport or a recycling center will reduce its pollution...</German>
+	<Italian>An aqueduct or a hospital will increase a city's health, but public transport or a recycling center will reduce its pollution...</Italian>
+	<Spanish>An aqueduct or a hospital will increase a city's health, but public transport or a recycling center will reduce its pollution...</Spanish>
+</TEXT>
+<TEXT>
+	<Tag>TXT_KEY_KMOD_HINT_2</Tag>
+	<English>The cultural influence of a city extends beyond the city's cultural border. If you are being culturally pressured by another civilization, consider getting more culture in all nearby cities; not just the cities being pressed.</English>
+	<French>The cultural influence of a city extends beyond the city's cultural border. If you are being culturally pressured by another civilization, consider getting more culture in all nearby cities; not just the cities being pressed.</French>
+	<German>The cultural influence of a city extends beyond the city's cultural border. If you are being culturally pressured by another civilization, consider getting more culture in all nearby cities; not just the cities being pressed.</German>
+	<Italian>The cultural influence of a city extends beyond the city's cultural border. If you are being culturally pressured by another civilization, consider getting more culture in all nearby cities; not just the cities being pressed.</Italian>
+	<Spanish>The cultural influence of a city extends beyond the city's cultural border. If you are being culturally pressured by another civilization, consider getting more culture in all nearby cities; not just the cities being pressed.</Spanish>
+</TEXT>
+<TEXT>
+	<Tag>TXT_KEY_KMOD_HINT_3</Tag>
+	<English>Forests and jungles help offset the pollution caused by your civilization. If you don't need to chop them down, consider keeping them to help "save the planet" in the future.</English>
+	<French>Forests and jungles help offset the pollution caused by your civilization. If you don't need to chop them down, consider keeping them to help "save the planet" in the future.</French>
+	<German>Forests and jungles help offset the pollution caused by your civilization. If you don't need to chop them down, consider keeping them to help "save the planet" in the future.</German>
+	<Italian>Forests and jungles help offset the pollution caused by your civilization. If you don't need to chop them down, consider keeping them to help "save the planet" in the future.</Italian>
+	<Spanish>Forests and jungles help offset the pollution caused by your civilization. If you don't need to chop them down, consider keeping them to help "save the planet" in the future.</Spanish>
+</TEXT>
+<TEXT>
+	<Tag>TXT_KEY_KMOD_HINT_4</Tag>
+	<English>If a rival civilization becomes fixated on world domination - beware! They may decide to attack you even if they appear friendly.</English>
+	<French>If a rival civilization becomes fixated on world domination - beware! They may decide to attack you even if they appear friendly.</French>
+	<German>If a rival civilization becomes fixated on world domination - beware! They may decide to attack you even if they appear friendly.</German>
+	<Italian>If a rival civilization becomes fixated on world domination - beware! They may decide to attack you even if they appear friendly.</Italian>
+	<Spanish>If a rival civilization becomes fixated on world domination - beware! They may decide to attack you even if they appear friendly.</Spanish>
+</TEXT>
